82
00:11:55,141 --> 00:11:57,301
Easy! Not while I'm holding a hot pot!

83
00:11:57,461 --> 00:11:58,761
Hina, the kitties are starving!

84
00:11:58,861 --> 00:11:59,941
Will you feed them, please?

85
00:12:00,681 --> 00:12:02,441
And set the table, okay?

86
00:12:02,581 --> 00:12:02,881
Okay!

87
00:12:04,341 --> 00:12:05,181
Guess what?

88
00:12:05,441 --> 00:12:06,361
Ray said he won!

89
00:12:06,641 --> 00:12:07,081
Really?

90
00:12:07,081 --> 00:12:08,101
Great!

91
00:12:08,681 --> 00:12:09,121
Great!

92
00:12:09,861 --> 00:12:11,301
Nom, nom, nom, nom, nom!

93
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:12,161
Nom, nom, nom!

94
00:12:18,961 --> 00:12:19,441
There!

95
00:12:19,741 --> 00:12:20,781
There you go, everyone!

96
00:12:22,141 --> 00:12:22,581
Wait!

97
00:12:22,841 --> 00:12:25,221
Hina, you're gonna put curry on the altar as an offering?

98
00:12:25,761 --> 00:12:26,201
Yeah!

99
00:12:26,341 --> 00:12:26,921
Why not?

100
00:12:27,261 --> 00:12:29,841
Mom and Grandma both used to love to eat curry, remember?

101
00:12:29,841 --> 00:12:32,821
Yeah, but isn't curry kind of an odd choice?

102
00:12:34,681 --> 00:12:37,541
Well, I guess you have a point. They did like curry.

103
00:12:38,261 --> 00:12:39,761
Well, I guess it's all right.

104
00:12:40,061 --> 00:12:41,601
Mama loves curry, too!

105
00:12:42,101 --> 00:12:45,941
Dear Mom and Grandma, you'll find that there's pork in tonight's curry.

106
00:12:48,141 --> 00:12:50,501
Well, everyone, let's dig in.

107
00:12:50,861 --> 00:12:52,541
All right! Thank you!

108
00:12:52,981 --> 00:12:54,721
For Eggie and Mama's pork, too!

109
00:12:54,941 --> 00:12:57,961
A whole egg? You sure you can eat that much?

110
00:12:57,961 --> 00:12:58,521
Yeah!

111
00:12:58,521 --> 00:13:00,141
Which leads us to our next story.

112
00:13:00,941 --> 00:13:05,981
Police found the badly bludgeoned body of Shizuo Unagawa in his home in Hibiya last night,

113
00:13:06,201 --> 00:13:08,621
which seems to have been caused by blunt force trauma.

114
00:13:09,381 --> 00:13:14,161
His eldest son, Tadashi, a university student who had been reported missing, has been arrested.

115
00:13:17,341 --> 00:13:21,201
According to the authorities, Tadashi is suspected of murdering his father

116
00:13:21,201 --> 00:13:24,761
by beating him with a hammer dozens of times in the head and face.

117
00:13:26,261 --> 00:13:28,001
Too bad about Mr. Koda.

118
00:13:28,001 --> 00:13:31,781
His entrance into the league after all this time was riding on that.

119
00:13:32,021 --> 00:13:34,281
Who knew his own son would beat him that badly?

120
00:13:34,861 --> 00:13:36,881
Although maybe it was satisfying to him in a way.

121
00:13:39,181 --> 00:13:42,461
Well, that is, only if he were his real son.

122
00:13:42,461 --> 00:13:57,521
Every move I made felt like I was punching him with my bare hands.

123
00:13:57,521 --> 00:13:58,141
It's...

124
00:13:58,141 --> 00:13:59,761
It's so vivid.

125
00:14:01,201 --> 00:14:03,201
Like I can still feel it, even now.

126
00:14:07,201 --> 00:14:07,521
Father...

127
00:14:07,521 --> 00:14:15,381
What's the matter, Ray?

128
00:14:15,381 --> 00:14:16,641
Are you cold?

129
00:14:18,201 --> 00:14:18,641
What?

130
00:14:19,621 --> 00:14:20,881
You don't look so good.

131
00:14:20,941 --> 00:14:21,501
Are you sick?

132
00:14:21,741 --> 00:14:22,921
Do you want me to get you something?

133
00:14:23,361 --> 00:14:24,201
Maybe some milk?

134
00:14:24,541 --> 00:14:24,941
Emergency!

135
00:14:24,941 --> 00:14:25,561
I can't see!

136
00:14:25,801 --> 00:14:26,841
Don't worry, I'm on it!

137
00:14:26,861 --> 00:14:27,121
Wait!

138
00:14:27,121 --> 00:14:28,461
I'll get some medicine, too!

139
00:14:30,801 --> 00:14:36,121
I'm sorry.

140
00:14:36,861 --> 00:14:37,781
I understand.

141
00:14:38,221 --> 00:14:39,261
Just eat what you can.

142
00:14:39,761 --> 00:14:40,841
Take your time, all right?

143
00:14:41,561 --> 00:14:43,181
But do try and eat a little.

144
00:14:43,181 --> 00:14:43,321
Huh?

145
00:14:52,041 --> 00:14:52,641
Okay.

146
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:02,041
Hey!

147
00:15:03,741 --> 00:15:05,181
What's with that kid?

148
00:15:05,581 --> 00:15:06,881
He fell asleep already?

149
00:15:07,441 --> 00:15:08,821
Talk about being rude.

150
00:15:09,501 --> 00:15:10,521
Aiden passed out.

151
00:15:10,761 --> 00:15:11,461
Pretty much.

152
00:15:11,461 --> 00:15:13,281
I don't think he's feeling well.

153
00:15:13,561 --> 00:15:15,301
When he finished dinner, he fell asleep.

154
00:15:16,441 --> 00:15:18,201
How did his match go today?

155
00:15:18,761 --> 00:15:19,861
Apparently he won.

156
00:15:20,201 --> 00:15:22,481
But when he got here, he looked so pale.

157
00:15:22,841 --> 00:15:24,281
And he barely ate a thing.

158
00:15:25,061 --> 00:15:26,161
That's too bad.

159
00:15:26,341 --> 00:15:28,221
I can imagine how exhausted he is.

160
00:15:29,061 --> 00:15:32,441
On top of that, he probably didn't get much sleep last night, either.

161
00:15:33,361 --> 00:15:34,221
All right, then.

162
00:15:34,301 --> 00:15:35,921
Just leave the boy here for tonight.

163
00:15:37,361 --> 00:15:39,601
I'll go back to the shop and sleep there.

164
00:15:39,601 --> 00:15:42,141
I'm making a batch of jam in the morning.

165
00:15:42,541 --> 00:15:44,061
Don't forget to lock up now.

166
00:15:44,301 --> 00:15:44,901
Of course.

167
00:15:45,241 --> 00:15:47,881
We'll help you make the jam and some pancakes, too.

168
00:15:48,521 --> 00:15:49,001
Okay.

169
00:15:49,141 --> 00:15:50,001
I'm counting on it.

170
00:15:50,521 --> 00:15:51,321
See you in the morning.

171
00:15:51,321 --> 00:15:54,521
I brought a blanket for you.

172
00:15:56,461 --> 00:15:58,381
He still has his glasses on.

173
00:15:58,381 --> 00:16:20,901
Good night.

174
00:16:20,901 --> 00:16:31,061
Ray Kiriyama.

175
00:16:31,061 --> 00:16:33,221
That's my name.

176
00:16:34,181 --> 00:16:36,821
In a small town by a big river,

177
00:16:37,821 --> 00:16:40,101
this is where my new life begins.

178
00:16:40,101 --> 00:16:44,981
Class C1, 5th Dunn, 17 years old.

179
00:16:46,021 --> 00:16:48,101
Profession, pro shogi player.

180
00:16:48,101 --> 00:17:06,041
Hey, are you an owl?

181
00:17:07,441 --> 00:17:09,201
No, it can't be, right?

182
00:17:09,901 --> 00:17:11,761
I mean, a magnificent white owl

183
00:17:11,761 --> 00:17:13,621
wouldn't just show up at somebody's house

184
00:17:13,621 --> 00:17:16,681
and stand there like that on the tatami mat.

185
00:17:17,681 --> 00:17:18,161
Wait.

186
00:17:18,641 --> 00:17:19,861
You're a cat, aren't you?

187
00:17:20,781 --> 00:17:21,441
Oh, no!

188
00:17:21,561 --> 00:17:23,201
I'm gonna be late for school again!

189
00:17:23,741 --> 00:17:24,781
Good morning, Ray!

190
00:17:25,241 --> 00:17:26,121
Good morning!

191
00:17:26,261 --> 00:17:26,921
What time is it?

192
00:17:27,021 --> 00:17:27,661
Here, hurry!

193
00:17:27,761 --> 00:17:28,241
Okay!

194
00:17:28,501 --> 00:17:29,301
Stir it up, please!

195
00:17:30,681 --> 00:17:31,081
Nowhere!

196
00:17:31,161 --> 00:17:31,601
Two eggs!

197
00:17:31,861 --> 00:17:32,081
Huh?

198
00:17:32,221 --> 00:17:32,621
Okay.

199
00:17:33,541 --> 00:17:33,981
Straight forward!

200
00:17:34,001 --> 00:17:34,461
Good morning!

201
00:17:34,721 --> 00:17:36,341
I woke you up like I said I would.

202
00:17:36,661 --> 00:17:37,921
Well, let's go, Momo.

203
00:17:37,921 --> 00:17:40,001
I'm awake, okay?

204
00:17:40,121 --> 00:17:40,701
Oh, no!

205
00:17:41,181 --> 00:17:43,181
Even though my sister woke me up,

206
00:17:43,421 --> 00:17:45,401
I can't believe I fell back to sleep!

207
00:17:45,681 --> 00:17:46,721
But first, a little more!

208
00:17:46,821 --> 00:17:47,521
This is the worst!

209
00:17:47,921 --> 00:17:49,021
I don't have time!

210
00:17:49,341 --> 00:17:51,461
But I just gotta have one more yummy ball!

211
00:17:51,581 --> 00:17:52,021
Wait!

212
00:17:52,201 --> 00:17:53,561
I thought you were running late!

213
00:17:53,621 --> 00:17:54,161
Oh, here!

214
00:17:54,401 --> 00:17:55,241
This is for you!

215
00:17:55,601 --> 00:17:56,321
It's your lunch!

216
00:17:56,421 --> 00:17:57,341
I know it's kind of big,

217
00:17:57,381 --> 00:17:58,521
but it shouldn't fall apart!

218
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:00,301
Oh, thank you.

219
00:18:00,481 --> 00:18:01,701
And here's a fish sausage!

220
00:18:02,041 --> 00:18:03,361
It'll go well with the rice ball!

221
00:18:04,201 --> 00:18:05,121
Okay, thanks!

222
00:18:05,341 --> 00:18:05,841
Gotta fly!

223
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,101
I have practice this morning!

224
00:18:07,101 --> 00:18:08,021
Take your time!

225
00:18:08,121 --> 00:18:08,361
See ya!

226
00:18:08,361 --> 00:18:08,701
Wait!

227
00:18:08,881 --> 00:18:09,961
What about the house key?

228
00:18:10,321 --> 00:18:10,741
Here!

229
00:18:11,021 --> 00:18:12,741
Please be sure to lock up when you leave!

230
00:18:12,941 --> 00:18:13,501
Wait a minute!

231
00:18:13,701 --> 00:18:14,481
If I have your key,

232
00:18:14,541 --> 00:18:15,621
then how will you get it later?

233
00:18:16,141 --> 00:18:16,781
That's fine!

234
00:18:16,881 --> 00:18:18,401
But we will find a way in somehow!

235
00:18:18,821 --> 00:18:19,241
Huh?

236
00:18:19,461 --> 00:18:20,761
But that doesn't work!

237
00:18:20,761 --> 00:18:33,921
I guess I'll go to school, too.

238
00:18:33,921 --> 00:18:37,941
I guess I'll go to school, too.

239
00:18:52,761 --> 00:18:53,241
Huh?

240
00:18:53,241 --> 00:18:54,981
What the hell, Kiriyama?

241
00:18:55,201 --> 00:18:56,421
That's a huge rice ball!

242
00:18:56,421 --> 00:18:57,701
Or is it a soccer ball?

243
00:18:58,161 --> 00:18:58,701
Aye, sir.

244
00:18:58,921 --> 00:19:00,061
Lucky you get rice.

245
00:19:00,381 --> 00:19:01,821
I'm broke till the end of the month,

246
00:19:01,901 --> 00:19:03,361
so this is all I can afford.

247
00:19:05,941 --> 00:19:07,761
So, how do you guys get paid?

248
00:19:08,101 --> 00:19:09,541
Is it like a monthly kind of thing?

249
00:19:09,901 --> 00:19:11,621
Or do they pay you after every match?

250
00:19:12,221 --> 00:19:13,461
Um, they pay monthly.

251
00:19:14,021 --> 00:19:15,641
They add up all the matches we've played,

252
00:19:15,901 --> 00:19:17,161
then deposit it in the bank.

253
00:19:17,461 --> 00:19:18,621
Well, I have to admit,

254
00:19:18,701 --> 00:19:20,181
I've been following you online.

255
00:19:21,221 --> 00:19:23,301
You've been on a big winning streak lately,

256
00:19:23,461 --> 00:19:25,261
so you must have a lot of matches.

257
00:19:26,061 --> 00:19:26,841
Let's see.

258
00:19:27,141 --> 00:19:28,001
Kiriyu tournament,

259
00:19:28,381 --> 00:19:29,341
Hyokushou tournament,

260
00:19:29,681 --> 00:19:30,421
rookie tournament.

261
00:19:30,861 --> 00:19:33,341
One, two, three...

262
00:19:33,961 --> 00:19:34,381
Oh.

263
00:19:36,641 --> 00:19:37,761
Look, Kiriyama.

264
00:19:37,761 --> 00:19:40,481
I don't mean to make a big deal about this,

265
00:19:40,921 --> 00:19:44,281
but do you think you're making more money than I am?

266
00:19:47,161 --> 00:19:53,341
That's it, dammit!

267
00:19:53,461 --> 00:19:55,281
I'm not gonna have lunch with you anymore!

268
00:19:55,381 --> 00:19:55,701
What?

269
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,061
I never really asked you to.

270
00:19:58,261 --> 00:19:59,161
If you don't like it,

271
00:19:59,221 --> 00:20:01,061
then hurry up and make friends here at school!

272
00:20:01,441 --> 00:20:02,201
I'm an adult.

273
00:20:02,381 --> 00:20:03,461
I have a lot to do.

274
00:20:09,461 --> 00:20:10,881
Even though he turned pro

275
00:20:10,881 --> 00:20:11,961
when he was in middle school

276
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:13,261
and could be called a genius,

277
00:20:13,961 --> 00:20:16,981
he's just a 17-year-old with issues like anyone else.

278
00:20:17,161 --> 00:20:21,121
I still can't help but wonder what he's thinking.

279
00:20:28,041 --> 00:20:28,961
Hi, welcome!

280
00:20:29,861 --> 00:20:31,541
Hello there, Rei. Welcome back.

281
00:20:31,801 --> 00:20:33,301
How was your lunch? Did you like it?

282
00:20:34,201 --> 00:20:35,021
Perfect timing.

283
00:20:35,681 --> 00:20:37,481
Maybe we can get you to help us out.

284
00:20:38,021 --> 00:20:39,461
I'll tie all the ribbons on,

285
00:20:39,721 --> 00:20:42,221
then you can put six in each box and stack them up.

286
00:20:42,301 --> 00:20:43,121
Okay, sure.

287
00:20:43,121 --> 00:20:43,901
Thanks a lot.

288
00:20:44,361 --> 00:20:45,741
Go ahead and wash your hands.

289
00:20:46,581 --> 00:20:48,841
Three smooth bean paste and three chunky.

290
00:20:49,161 --> 00:20:49,601
Got it.

291
00:20:49,741 --> 00:20:51,281
Isn't that cute wrapping paper?

292
00:20:51,761 --> 00:20:52,761
It looks expensive.

293
00:20:53,401 --> 00:20:55,041
It's not printed, is it?

294
00:20:55,241 --> 00:20:57,181
Actually, Hina made it by herself.

295
00:20:57,461 --> 00:20:58,161
Pretty impressive.

296
00:20:58,521 --> 00:20:59,341
Potato prints!

297
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:01,641
I carved the pattern into a sweet potato.

298
00:21:02,021 --> 00:21:02,961
Then I printed them.

299
00:21:03,221 --> 00:21:03,941
Cute, huh?

300
00:21:04,701 --> 00:21:07,021
These are for Grandpa's friend, the calligraphy teacher.

301
00:21:07,441 --> 00:21:09,761
He's going to be celebrating his 70th birthday,

302
00:21:10,061 --> 00:21:11,161
the big 7-0.

303
00:21:11,921 --> 00:21:14,921
He used to teach Hina when she was in elementary school.

304
00:21:15,681 --> 00:21:18,021
So this is her special present to him.

305
00:21:18,881 --> 00:21:21,701
I must say, you're indeed a fortunate man.

306
00:21:21,961 --> 00:21:24,541
Having grandchildren willing to help is a blessing.

307
00:21:24,921 --> 00:21:25,781
That's for sure.

308
00:21:26,181 --> 00:21:28,761
You're a lucky man to have their devotions, Soma-ji.

309
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,801
You don't know the half of it.

310
00:21:31,121 --> 00:21:32,681
The little one always gets in the way,

311
00:21:32,761 --> 00:21:34,341
and she's so noisy I can't think.

312
00:21:34,601 --> 00:21:35,421
Look, Grandpa!

313
00:21:35,821 --> 00:21:37,201
I made it by myself!

314
00:21:37,321 --> 00:21:37,981
Oh, wow!

315
00:21:38,181 --> 00:21:38,941
Watchable, Momo!

316
00:21:39,361 --> 00:21:40,101
It's a flower!

317
00:21:40,101 --> 00:21:41,141
Sorry about that.

318
00:21:41,581 --> 00:21:44,221
Grandpa's a bit of a softie when it comes to us grandkids.

319
00:21:44,681 --> 00:21:45,901
Just a bit, huh?

320
00:21:47,021 --> 00:21:49,101
Well, I'm off to deliver all these.

321
00:21:49,901 --> 00:21:52,801
I'm going to stay for the party, too, so I might be home late.

322
00:21:52,901 --> 00:21:53,821
Be sure to lock up.

323
00:21:54,341 --> 00:21:54,741
Bye!

324
00:21:58,401 --> 00:21:59,921
All right, let's get going.

325
00:22:00,441 --> 00:22:01,901
Are you having dinner with us tonight?

326
00:22:02,521 --> 00:22:03,721
Thanks a lot for offering,

327
00:22:04,161 --> 00:22:05,761
but I really need to go home tonight.

328
00:22:06,201 --> 00:22:07,141
I have to prepare.

329
00:22:07,541 --> 00:22:09,821
I have another match, so I should go.

330
00:22:10,201 --> 00:22:12,141
Oh, you've got a lot of matches.

331
00:22:12,381 --> 00:22:12,981
Good luck, Ray!

332
00:22:13,141 --> 00:22:14,181
Good luck, Ray!

333
00:22:14,501 --> 00:22:14,941
Thanks.

334
00:22:15,721 --> 00:22:16,941
And thanks again for my lunch.

335
00:22:17,661 --> 00:22:18,521
It was so good.

336
00:22:18,521 --> 00:22:19,701
Then have this.

337
00:22:19,941 --> 00:22:21,381
One of our baked crescent moons.

338
00:22:21,741 --> 00:22:23,521
Still warm and really fresh.

339
00:22:24,661 --> 00:22:25,221
Bye.

340
00:22:25,541 --> 00:22:26,481
Thanks for everything.

341
00:22:27,321 --> 00:22:28,441
Come over anytime.

342
00:22:28,781 --> 00:22:29,541
We'll be waiting.

343
00:22:30,021 --> 00:22:30,621
Good night.

344
00:22:30,821 --> 00:22:32,021
See you later!

345
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:45,741
It still hasn't come.

346
00:22:45,741 --> 00:22:53,741
Could this be what you're looking for by any chance?

347
00:22:54,121 --> 00:22:55,261
Ray, Kiriyama.

348
00:22:56,001 --> 00:22:56,601
Determined!

349
00:22:57,081 --> 00:22:57,441
Who?

350
00:22:57,441 --> 00:22:58,201
There's only one of the best.

351
00:22:58,221 --> 00:22:58,601
Touchdown.

352
00:22:58,681 --> 00:22:59,161
We'll be right back.

353
00:22:59,181 --> 00:22:59,701
We'll be right back.

354
00:22:59,981 --> 00:23:00,241
See you later.

355
00:23:00,321 --> 00:23:00,861
Bye.

356
00:23:01,581 --> 00:23:01,701
See you later.

357
00:23:04,481 --> 00:23:04,821
Have a great day.

358
00:23:04,821 --> 00:23:05,741
There's a great day.

359
00:23:05,841 --> 00:23:06,281
Quindi.

360
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:39,711
Well, I'm very sad to say that it looks like Rei would rather have instant noodles instead of our home cooking.

361
00:24:40,031 --> 00:24:42,831
Don't be so cold to a buddy! We're best friends, remember?

362
00:24:43,271 --> 00:24:44,611
Oh, hey, Rei!

363
00:24:44,971 --> 00:24:47,311
Help me, Mr. Hanaoka!

364
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:49,471
I found you, Rei!

365
00:24:51,851 --> 00:24:56,591
March comes in like a lion. Don't miss the next episode. I'm counting on you.

366
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
I'm counting on you.

